---
---

<section id="tracks" class="tracks">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Two tracks, twenty seats</p>
        <h2>Pick the one you can <span class="gold">actually finish</span>.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="deck">
        Both tracks build. The difference is how much of the town agent you
        own by 19 November.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-2up">
      <div class="card track">
        <span class="badge">Track A</span>
        <h3>Foundations &mdash; and you still build.</h3>
        <p class="body">
          You learn how an agent is put together, then ship one small useful
          agent of your own. Scoped in the first week so it can be finished
          in nine.
        </p>
        <p class="who">
          Right if you are a student, or new to this, and want the ground
          under you before you carry weight.
        </p>
        <div class="walk">
          <span>You walk out with</span>
          <span class="ans">One agent, running</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card card-gold track">
        <span class="badge">Track B</span>
        <h3>You own a piece of the town agent, and ship it.</h3>
        <p class="body">
          A named layer of the real thing is yours &mdash; a tool, a data
          path, a guardrail. It goes live with your name on the commit, or
          it does not go live.
        </p>
        <p class="who">
          Right if you already write code for a living and want something
          harder than a tutorial.
        </p>
        <div class="walk">
          <span>You walk out with</span>
          <span class="ans">A shipped layer in production</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .tracks { background: var(--surface-page); }

  .head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: end;
    gap: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .deck { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; max-width: 38ch; }

  .grid-2up {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .track { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }

  .badge {
    align-self: start;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-on-gold);
    background: var(--gradient-gold);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 6px 14px;
  }

  .track h3 { margin: 0; }
  .body { margin: 0; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: none; }
  .who { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-subtle); max-width: none; }

  .walk {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
  }

  .ans { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--gold-300); text-align: right; }
</style>
